(Regular file overflow: a fixed buffer too small for a regular file must signal overflow and hold exactly capacity bytes.)

(Create a 20-byte regular file.)
open a file for writing called w at "./b342_data.txt".
Write "01234567890123456789" to w.
Close w.

(A 10-byte fixed buffer cannot hold 20 bytes; the read fills exactly with more data ahead, so overflow is signalled.)
a buffer called buf is 10 bytes in size.
open a file for reading called f at "./b342_data.txt".
Read from f into buf.
On error print "overflow".
Print "got: ".
Print buf.
Print "size: ".
Print buf's size.
Close f.
Delete the file "./b342_data.txt".